From a46b34fbf372ec0f53ddbe5967a5e3dd374391d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 01:43:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove dead shadow-map flag, extract themes, drop flagpole,
 smooth theme transitions

- Remove renderer.shadowMap.enabled: nothing cast or received shadows,
  so it was pure wasted GPU work.
- Move the 13 theme palette definitions out of App.vue into src/themes.js.
- Remove the flagpole/finial meshes; the flag's hoist edge is already
  pinned by the shader, so the pole wasn't structurally necessary.
- Make theme-transition easing frame-rate independent (delta-time based)
  and blend uRainbowMode continuously in the fragment shader instead of
  hard-switching at a 0.5 threshold, so crossfading in/out of rainbow
  themes is smooth instead of an instant pop.
